


STAT(1)             UNIX Programmer's Manual                STAT(1)



NAME
     stat - display file status

SYNOPSIS
     stat file ...

DESCRIPTION
     _S_t_a_t displays the status of each _f_i_l_e: name, size in bytes,
     blocks allocated (st_blocks), type (regular file, directory
     or other), a mode string in the shape of ls -l, the i-number
     (as printed by ls -i), and the modification time.  On a
     mounted ProDOS volume these are synthesized as
     mount_prodos(8) describes.

     This is an FGX-native tool (there is no BSD stat(1) of this
     vintage); output is shaped after the modern stat utilities.

SEE ALSO
     ls(1), touch(1), strmode(3), mount_prodos(8)

